Attached: pow_research_kernel_2026-09-20.zip

This is the runnable additive POW research kernel built against the current
prx0r/powpowpow architecture.

Included:

   - 64-source data asset registry (30 P0 / 27 P1 / 7 P2), with cadence,
   recoverability, access mode, variables and model mappings
   - Richards diffusion + adoption=E2=86=92BOM demand bridge
   - Leontief production-network shock propagation
   - LP shadow-price / bottleneck solver
   - finite-shock systemic criticality stress tests
   - complementarity/synergy screen with formal PID/JIDT path
   - installed-base maintenance cohorts
   - labor/skill pressure
   - lead/lag + optional PCMCI+
   - scarcity-migration scenario runner
   - POW-compatible raw archival/normalization bridge
   - no-key collector examples
   - dependency/BOM compiler specification
   - probe schedule, source access setup, research foundation, integration
   plan, DuckDB views and tests

Validation: 7/7 tests passed. Installer tested non-destructively against an
existing-POW-shaped checkout.

Core thesis: record technological state deeply enough to reconstruct how
scarcity migrates after capability/cost shocks, then backtest the causal
latency from physical evidence through supply, labor, narrative and markets=
.

